; 5 - ORG and RMB in qaflisp's first pass
; ORG and RMB determine addresses. qaflisp evaluates them in its first
; pass, when later labels and some constants are not known yet.
; qaflisp reports this as "Forward reference" - or as "Phase error"
; at a completely different line. The live check shows the cause directly.
;
; Try it:
;   - Assemble with F7: qaflisp reports only lines 25, 27 and 29 -
;     line 27 as "Phase error" at the label Buf6. Lines 26 and 30 get
;     lost in the follow-up error. The live check shows each cause.
;   - Comment out all ERROR lines but one (Ctrl+/) and assemble:
;     this shows qaflisp's message for each case on its own.
;   - Line 23 (RMB Count) is OK although Count comes only in line 33:
;     a constant with a plain number may come later, a label may not.

N           EQU     4               ; OK
Offset      EQU     Start+4         ; OK: but contains a label
Late        EQU     Size            ; OK: but uses Size, defined later

            ORG     $20
Start       NOP                     ; OK
Buf1        RMB     N*2             ; OK: number constant
Buf2        RMB     Count           ; OK: later constant with a plain number
Buf3        RMB     Start+2-Start   ; OK: labels from above, used directly
Buf4        RMB     End-Start       ; ERROR: End is further down
Buf5        RMB     Offset-$20      ; ERROR: Offset contains a label
Buf6        RMB     Late            ; ERROR: Late uses Size, defined later
            ORG     Start+$40       ; OK: label from above, used directly
            ORG     Far             ; ERROR: Forward reference
            ORG     Offset          ; ERROR: Offset contains a label
End         NOP                     ; OK

Count       EQU     3               ; OK
Size        EQU     2               ; OK
Far         EQU     $80             ; OK
